      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors present the currently available data on the socioeconomic status, social isolation, social support, and associated personality changes considered to be risk factors of coronary heart disease (CHD). In addition, socioeconomic conditions of the family during the patient's childhood contributing to the evolvement and progression of CHD are reviewed. Information is provided about the role of combination of common somatic risk factors of CHD and socio-psychologic peculiarities of the patients in the development of CHD."},
      "ArticleTitle": "[The role of psychosocial risk factors in evolvement and progression of coronary heart disease].",
